    "body": "The BIP-375 reference validator crashes with an `AssertionError`, instead of rejecting the PSBT, on three malformed inputs: no `PSBT_IN_WITNESS_UTXO` and no `PSBT_IN_NON_WITNESS_UTXO`; `PSBT_IN_OUTPUT_INDEX` past the end of the non-witness UTXO; a P2SH scriptPubKey without `PSBT_IN_REDEEM_SCRIPT`. All three reach the asserts in `validator/inputs.py` from `is_input_eligible`. Measured on master `d71d6068` by mutating one valid vector at a time.\n\nThe first commit raises `ValueError` there and lets `validate_bip375_psbt` report it as a failed check; `test_runner.py` still passes 44 of 44. The second adds one invalid vector per case, listed in the BIP table under ECDH Coverage, the check that rejects them: 47 of 47 with the fix, and each vector alone crashes the master validator. A separate commit sets Version 0.1.4 with its changelog entry: each of my open BIP-375 pull requests (#2315, #2316, #2317, #2324) does the same, and whichever lands first keeps 0.1.4 while the others rebase to the next version.\n\n*Made with my usual tools: a computer, the Internet and an LLM. The mistakes, as usual, are all mine.*\n",
